7426	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-383f0554bf7bf6542d1f945fb88717a8","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:45:04.324Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process identity addresses the ISSUE's false-stop root cause in both CLI and shell.","evidence":"The ISSUE identifies loss of the original PID after run-file removal. waitForStop returns true on '!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile)', and stopDaemonWith immediately returns '{ stopped: true, forced: false }'. The shell uses the same file-disappearance condition and rereads the PID in force_stop_daemon. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"Implement the retained-target checks in both paths as proposed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.2","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The design fulfills the ISSUE's entire diagnostic fix intent.","evidence":"The ISSUE requires that 'the reason it did not exit on 2026-10-13 is diagnosed and recorded'. The design explicitly leaves that cause unproven and substitutes a controlled blocked-exit reproduction. That is a scope change, although an honest treatment of the available evidence. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Explicitly obtain agreement to defer the historical diagnosis and record it as unresolved rather than treating ac4 as full satisfaction of the ISSUE.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Shutdown removes run files and logs bye before attempting normal process exit, and repeated signals do not retry shutdown.","evidence":"createShutdown executes 'await parts.closeStores(); end.clearPid(); parts.log.info(\\'bye\\'); clearTimeout(backstop); exitRespectingStoreHealth(...)'. Healthy exit calls deps.exit(code), whose real implementation is process.exit(code). The 'if (started)' branch logs and returns. index.ts closes the request server in stopBackgroundWork. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"Keep the distinction between run-file removal and process termination.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The named production stop and shutdown functions are the relevant change sites, with restart already awaiting the CLI stop outcome.","evidence":"daemon.ts wires realStopDeps.waitForStop to lifecycle.ts and owns stopDaemonWith and forced cleanup. scripts/daemon-ctl.sh shares signal_stop, wait_for_daemon_stop and force_stop_daemon between stop and stale-start handling. maintenance.restart awaits deps.stopDaemon() and returns on rejection before startDaemon(). index.ts constructs createShutdown with queue and store cleanup callbacks. [files: src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"Include both shell stop and stale-start flows in retained-target wiring; implement the watchdog default inside shutdown.ts or update its index.ts construction site explicitly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing shutdown is idempotent and skips queue waiting and unsafe store close when lock loss is detected.","evidence":"createShutdown guards with 'if (started)' and sets started before cleanup. The initial locks-lost branch schedules endAfterStoreFailure and returns; the post-drain health check also calls endAfterStoreFailure before closeStores. Existing tests assert no close or normal exit on these paths. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts]","action":"Keep these branches and add assertions that repeated signals arm only one watchdog.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Watchdog launch failure still provides bounded daemon termination by self-killing after explicit cleanup.","evidence":"The proposed failure response waits until 'after explicit cleanup' to self-kill. Actual cleanup awaits parts.closeStores(), and index.ts invokes native DuckDB, graph and Lance closes there. shutdown.ts explicitly describes a store close that 'would then never return'. With no ready watchdog, a native cleanup block prevents reaching killSelf and prevents the in-process timer from running. A CLI deadline cannot protect a shutdown initiated solely by SIGTERM. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"On watchdog readiness failure, take a synchronous diagnostic/self-kill path before potentially blocking native cleanup, or establish another independent termination mechanism first. Test launch failure combined with blocked cleanup.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping contains regression scenarios for retained targets, independent termination, replacement safety and the explicitly limited diagnostic evidence.","evidence":"The design maps ac1 to CLI and shell run-file deletion while the target lives, ac2 to blocked exit and healthy watchdog termination, ac3 to identity/replacement failures and restart refusal, and ac4 to recorded reproduction plus the historical caveat. Existing daemon-stop.test.ts uses a fixed PID and injected wait result; daemon-stop-forced.test.ts keeps run files present until forced cleanup, so these existing tests do not cover the reported false-success trigger. The proposed deletion scenario would expose that trigger. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop-forced.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the proposed regressions using real waitForStop and disposable processes as well as dependency fakes. Add watchdog-readiness-failure plus blocked-cleanup coverage; resolve the ac4 scope discrepancy before treating acceptance as complete.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T13:45:04.324Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
