6833	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-46f8b034a9e1681939e77302b0dc4067","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:00:43.159Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process identity and independently bounding shutdown addresses both termination defects in the ISSUE.","evidence":"waitForStop succeeds on absent files; stopDaemonWith reads the PID again after waiting. createShutdown clears run files before exit and clears its timer before exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained identity and independent helper cover these failure mechanisms. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Implement both protections together.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.2","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The design leaves nothing out of the ISSUE fix intent.","evidence":"ISSUE.md requires that 'the reason it did not exit on 2026-10-13 is diagnosed and recorded.' The design instead explicitly leaves that diagnosis unproven and substitutes a controlled blocked-exit reproduction. The historical smoke record reports symptoms and semaphore errors, not an established cause. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md, docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/smoke.md]","action":"Explicitly resolve this scope change with the user, or add an investigation deliverable; do not treat the synthetic reproduction as establishing the historical cause.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CLI and shell currently infer stop success from disappearing run files, and shutdown can remove those files before process exit.","evidence":"waitForStop contains 'if (!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile)) return true'; the shell uses the equivalent file/socket condition. createShutdown calls 'end.clearPid()', logs 'bye', then calls exitRespectingStoreHealth; clearPid removes both files. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/lifecycle.ts]","action":"Replace file disappearance as sufficient evidence with retained-process termination verification.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The identified existing functions cover stop waiting, forced termination, and shutdown orchestration without requiring a changed restart API.","evidence":"stopDaemonWith wires lifecycle.waitForStop through realStopDeps. maintenance.restart awaits stopDaemon and returns on rejection before startDaemon. Shell cmd_stop and the stale-daemon branch of cmd_start share signal_stop, wait_for_daemon_stop and force_stop_daemon. createShutdown owns cleanup and can supply a default watchdog seam without changing its caller's API. [files: src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts]","action":"Wire identity through both shell entry paths and update StopDeps test fixtures; add the new helper as a compiled runtime module.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Orderly healthy shutdown, lock-loss close avoidance, and shutdown reentrancy protection are existing behaviors compatible with the proposed watchdog.","evidence":"createShutdown guards with 'if (started)' before cleanup. Healthy shutdown waits for queueDone then closeStores and normal exit. Initial or post-drain locks-lost health skips closeStores and invokes endAfterStoreFailure. Existing tests assert normal exit order, repeated-signal suppression and SIGKILL without unsafe close. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts]","action":"Keep these branches after watchdog readiness and retain the existing contract tests.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The planned tests distinguish the termination and identity protections in ac1–ac3 from the current implementation.","evidence":"Existing stop tests fake a fixed PID and boolean wait result; forced-stop integration children retain their run files. The proposed disappearing-file/live-process, changed-start-marker, replacement ownership and blocked-exit cases exercise failures these fixtures omit. Existing restart tests already assert no start after stop rejection. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop-forced.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Add the proposed regression cases and assert process exit independently of run-file disappearance, including shell restart ordering.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every mapped criterion has a proving test, including ac4's recorded reproduction and diagnostic caveat.","evidence":"The ac4 mapping says 'Record reproducible blocked-exit evidence and state explicitly that the historical 2026-10-13 native cause is not established.' Listed integration tests assert bounded termination, but none asserts that reproduction evidence is recorded or that the resulting record contains the historical-cause caveat. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Specify an evidence artifact and a check for its reproduction details and caveat, or classify this explicitly as a required manual documentation acceptance check.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T14:00:43.159Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
