534	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"bf89487ca83b43a2aa4886ef085c5250","actor":{"id":"codex:shutdown-design","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:02:46.991Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":3,"contentHash":"312bde4ec56d41a9aa10149aabcb9e180b485002e9a27dc32f8c673523c34cc6"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Address round-2 test finding: specify required manual investigation-evidence acceptance; retain the unresolved historical-diagnosis scope decision."},"addresses":"all"}}
727	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"e7826ce9b09742dd9cbec6665b2fb133","actor":{"id":"codex:shutdown-design","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T14:52:41.678Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":4,"contentHash":"f48b9014511ec0d942181c2fc3db188d17418a64de6deeb50e5a042159871f84"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Stakeholder decision on 2026-10-24: implement reliable termination now; defer the original 2026-10-13 native-hang diagnosis. Controlled reproduction and diagnostic documentation are required for this work, but do not establish the original historical cause. Historical diagnosis remains deferred follow-up, not a completed acceptance claim."},"addresses":"all"}}
5577	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-ca5a7798d35a28a90d902b678a86b306","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:09:21.611Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process identity and adding independent shutdown protection address the two termination faults stated in the ISSUE.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies file-based stop success and a process surviving after 'bye' as separate faults. lifecycle.ts returns true when both run files disappear; shutdown.ts clears those files before calling exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained target and independent helper directly address these paths. The design explicitly records the stakeholder's deferral of historical diagnosis. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Keep historical diagnosis explicitly deferred rather than claiming the controlled reproduction proves it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today, stop can report success after run-file deletion without observing the original process exit, and forced stop rereads the PID file.","evidence":"waitForStop contains 'if (!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile)) return true'. stopDaemonWith immediately returns '{ stopped: true, forced: false }' on that result, and its later livePid() reads deps.pidFromFile(). The shell wait uses the same absence rule and force_stop_daemon rereads PID_FILE. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"Capture identity before shutdown and retain it throughout waiting and forced termination.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The listed change sites cover all run-file deletion paths needed to guarantee that replacement run files are never deleted.","evidence":"The omitted src/daemon/lifecycle.ts clearPid() unconditionally executes 'rmSync(PATHS.pidFile)' and 'rmSync(PATHS.sockFile)'. The omitted server.ts close() awaits server closure and then executes 'rmSync(this.socketPath)'. index.ts invokes 'void server.close()', while shutdown.ts later calls end.clearPid(). Caller-side ownership checks cannot prevent these daemon-side deletions if replacement files appear during shutdown. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Include daemon lifecycle cleanup and request-server close in the ownership design. Specify how each deletion verifies ownership, and test replacement files appearing while the original daemon drains.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Store-health-aware termination and shutdown reentrancy are existing behaviors that can be retained around the watchdog.","evidence":"createShutdown guards repeated signals with 'if (started)' and returns. For locks-lost health it skips queue waiting and store close, calling endAfterStoreFailure; it checks health again after queue drain. exitRespectingStoreHealth chooses self-SIGKILL for locks-lost and normal exit otherwise. Existing tests assert these paths and cleanup order. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts]","action":"Keep these branches and assertions when introducing watchdog readiness.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed tests give a regression-sensitive check for each revised acceptance criterion.","evidence":"ac1 proposes live-target tests after run-file deletion for CLI and shell; current wait implementations would incorrectly succeed. ac2 proposes a blocked exit-hook child, which the current in-process backstop cannot rescue. ac3 proposes PID reuse and identity-failure cases absent from the current command-only verification. ac4 explicitly requires manual evidence inspection, rather than claiming an automated historical diagnosis. Existing daemon-stop and shell integration fixtures provide suitable extension points, but do not yet exercise these new cases. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop-forced.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-ctl-forced-stop.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Implement the proposed tests and manual evidence checklist; include the daemon-side replacement-file race identified above. No new tests or reproduction evidence were executed during this review.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":4,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T15:09:21.611Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
