541	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"cbe91f7179a3459cb102a8f063b0e0f8","actor":{"id":"codex:shutdown-design","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:21:15.625Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":6,"contentHash":"34ac98eefc9c42dd7c36dd02836a14a1dab2efdc365d5aeeb450736d3b1f7669"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Address review cycle2 round2 HIGH: an orphaned run-file guard is a stop/restart failure, never a successful stop followed by a failing replacement launch."},"addresses":"all"}}
7431	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-7fa25e0f30192f7f005e7081dc6731cb","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:21:18.057Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process identity and adding independent termination protection addresses the two operational faults stated in the ISSUE.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies file-based stop success and a process surviving after 'bye'. waitForStop returns true from absent files; stopDaemonWith trusts that result and rereads the PID only afterward. createShutdown clears run files, logs 'bye', clears its backstop and invokes exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained target and external watchdog address these paths. Historical diagnosis is explicitly deferred in the supplied design. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Keep historical diagnosis recorded as deferred rather than completed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current stop logic can declare success after run files disappear while the original daemon remains alive.","evidence":"waitForStop checks '!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile)' and returns true without retaining a PID. stopDaemonWith immediately returns '{ stopped: true, forced: false }' on that answer. The shell wait uses the equivalent file-absence condition. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"Implement retained-target checks in both stop paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The current shutdown has a closeStores ordering deadlock caused by awaiting server.close before disconnecting clients.","evidence":"stopBackgroundWork calls 'void server.close();'; it does not await completion. closeStores subsequently calls 'await server.flushPendingWrites(1000); server.disconnectClients();'. Although IpcServer.close awaits the server close callback internally, its caller does not block closeStores on that promise. The proposed awaited close could introduce this dependency, but it is not the current ordering deadlock claimed in section 3.3. [files: src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Describe disconnect-before-awaited-close as a requirement introduced by the new serialized shutdown sequence; remove the claim that this deadlock exists today.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed production change sites cover the existing managed run-file writers and stop/restart paths.","evidence":"Direct reads and repository-wide searches locate PID publication and stale cleanup in daemon/lifecycle.ts, socket removal in IpcServer.listen/close, startup and shutdown composition in daemon/index.ts, terminal cleanup in daemon/shutdown.ts, CLI removals in services/lifecycle.ts and daemon.ts, and shell signal/wait/force-stop operations in daemon-ctl.sh. maintenance.restart awaits stop and returns on failure before start. Fatal cleanup delegates through exitRespectingStoreHealth and the shared EndDeps path. The analyzer was attempted but failed with an invalid response-schema error; these findings use direct reads. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/fatal.ts, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"Apply the ownership contract to the shared terminal cleanup path so fatal callers inherit it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Store-health-aware termination, shutdown reentrancy protection and the StopOutcome shape are existing behaviors that the proposed seams can preserve.","evidence":"createShutdown guards repeated signals with 'if (started)' and skips queue waiting/store close when health is locks-lost. endAfterStoreFailure writes synchronously and calls killSelf; exitRespectingStoreHealth calls exit only for healthy stores. StopOutcome contains stopped:true, forced:boolean and optional pid. Existing shutdown tests assert skipped close, self-kill, healthy exit and ignored repeat signals; the design retains these branches and result fields. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts]","action":"Retain these assertions while adding watchdog and ownership seams, including failure during queue drain.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance mapping supplies regression scenarios for ac1–ac3 and an explicit manual evidence check for ac4.","evidence":"The design specifies file disappearance while the original process lives for ac1, a blocked exit hook and healthy watchdog control for ac2, and reused identity/replacement plus restart refusal for ac3. Existing daemon-stop tests use injected StopDeps and restart dependencies; shell tests run the actual script against disposable processes, supporting the proposed extensions. ac4 explicitly requires manual inspection of reproduction evidence rather than claiming an automated test. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-ctl-forced-stop.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts]","action":"Implement the proposed scenarios; make process exit, preserved foreign files and absence of a replacement start explicit assertions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The required ac4 reproduction evidence has already been recorded and can be verified.","evidence":"The story directory contains LLD.md and sequence-diagram.html, but no shutdown-investigation.md. No controlled reproduction command, timestamp, identity, deadlines, healthy-control results or source logs could be inspected at the required path. The design correctly treats this as future acceptance work. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/shutdown-investigation.md]","action":"Create and review shutdown-investigation.md with the specified evidence before accepting ac4; retain the historical-cause caveat.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":6,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T15:21:18.057Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
