6110	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-5e12ea0c0f39e2a3b3f82f7777eeac62","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T15:32:58.933Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process identity and enforcing termination independently addresses the two operational faults stated in the ISSUE.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies file-based stop success and a process surviving after 'bye'. waitForStop returns true on absent PID/socket paths; stopDaemonWith accepts that result immediately. createShutdown clears the PID, logs 'bye', clears its timer and then invokes exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained-target wait and independent watchdog address those paths. Historical diagnosis is explicitly deferred in the supplied design, rather than claimed complete. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Keep the historical diagnosis visible as deferred scope; do not mark the original ISSUE's diagnostic intent completed.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current stop logic loses its original target when shutdown removes the PID file, and server close currently does not block store cleanup.","evidence":"stopDaemonWith calls requestShutdown before reading livePid for fallback, and livePid rereads pidFromFile. waitForStop repeatedly reads the PID file and returns true when both paths disappear. index.ts calls 'void server.close()' in stopBackgroundWork; closeStores later flushes writes and disconnects clients. IpcServer.close awaits the native close callback before its explicit socket removal. Analyzer drill-down was attempted but failed with shaper-llm-unavailable and an invalid response-schema error; these conclusions use direct reads. [files: src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"Preserve capture-before-request ordering and move client disconnection ahead of any newly awaited server close.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed production files cover the existing stop, restart, publication and run-file deletion implementations.","evidence":"Caller and writer searches locate waitForStop's production invocation in daemon.ts; restart in maintenance.ts; PID write/stale cleanup in daemon/lifecycle.ts; socket publication/removal in server.ts; shutdown wiring in index.ts; final cleanup through shutdown.ts; and shell stop, forced stop and restart in daemon-ctl.sh. These files are all listed. The watchdog and shared guard are explicitly new components. [files: src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, src/daemon/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/fatal.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"Implement the ownership contract through the shared cleanup dependencies so fatal and startup-error callers inherit it, and update affected test fixtures.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Store-health-aware termination, shutdown idempotence and restart failure propagation are existing behaviors the design can preserve.","evidence":"createShutdown's started guard suppresses duplicate cleanup. A locks-lost health result bypasses queue/store close and invokes endAfterStoreFailure; exitRespectingStoreHealth selects SIGKILL instead of process.exit for that state. maintenance.restart catches stop failure and returns before startDaemon. StopOutcome contains stopped:true, forced:boolean and optional pid, matching the proposed unchanged shape. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts]","action":"Retain these branches while adding watchdog readiness and ownership checks; keep ownership conflicts on the throwing stop path.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed regression scenarios distinguish the unfixed behavior for ac1–ac3 and define a concrete manual acceptance check for ac4.","evidence":"Existing daemon-stop tests use a fixed PID and a mocked wait result, so they do not cover disappearing run files or PID reuse. Existing shell tests keep run files for stubborn children and immediately exit healthy children. The proposed retained-identity, blocked-exit, replacement-process and orphan-guard scenarios exercise these missing failures. ac4 explicitly requires inspection of reproduction evidence and a historical-cause caveat rather than claiming an automated test. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-ctl-forced-stop.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/LLD.md]","action":"Add the proposed regressions, including real waitForStop coverage, and perform the ac4 evidence review before acceptance. This finding verifies test design, not implementation or passing results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":5,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T15:32:58.933Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
