685	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"ffe1a5610b8046c4a90cf868e96f63e8","actor":{"id":"codex:shutdown-design","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:27:31.334Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":9,"contentHash":"f92c4a1b5e8fff754b708b239c5ade92ec8262b2a487fc9bd5198838726fd379"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Correct refinement review MED: the real build uses root copy-assets.mjs. Define compilation in a root build-process-broker.mjs invoked by package.json before the existing copy-assets step. Stable process capabilities and new evidence remain proposed implementation work, not already-proven results."},"addresses":"all"}}
6453	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-68c88696b1638314f7fc4d26fb7d9e44","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T16:27:34.248Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process capability across shutdown and independently enforcing termination addresses the ISSUE's two termination faults.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies file-based stop success and a process surviving after 'bye'. stopDaemonWith currently returns immediately when waitForStop succeeds; createShutdown clears the PID, logs 'bye', clears its backstop, then calls exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained target and independent watchdog address those paths. Historical diagnosis is explicitly deferred in this revision rather than claimed complete. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Keep historical diagnosis recorded as deferred ISSUE scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CLI and shell stop waits currently infer successful termination from disappearing run files and lose the original PID before forced termination.","evidence":"waitForStop returns true on '!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile)'. stopDaemonWith reads livePid only after RPC failure or the wait, rather than capturing it beforehand. The shell wait likewise returns when PID/socket disappear, and force_stop_daemon rereads PID_FILE. index.ts starts 'void server.close()' without awaiting it. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"Implement capture before RPC or signal in both stop implementations.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The change-site list covers the existing ownership implementation and callers affected by changing cleanup contracts.","evidence":"The list omits src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts, which already implements acquireRunFileGuard, runFileGuardConflict and removeOwnedRunFile, including 'guard.assertOwned(); ... unlinkSync(path)'. It also omits the store-child fixture, which calls writePid(), constructs createShutdown and supplies 'stopBackgroundWork: () => { queue.stop(); void server.close(); }'. These existing foundations and callers must be reconciled with the revised capability and ownership contracts. [files: src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-run-files.test.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/helpers/store-child.ts, src/daemon/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Add the existing shared guard module, its tests and the store-child shutdown fixture to the explicit change/compatibility audit; specify reuse versus revision.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Store-health-aware termination, shutdown reentrancy protection and withholding CLI restart after stop failure are existing behaviors that the proposed contracts preserve.","evidence":"createShutdown uses a 'started' guard and skips queue/store cleanup on locks-lost. endAfterStoreFailure writes synchronously and invokes killSelf; exitRespectingStoreHealth uses normal exit only for healthy stores. maintenance.restart returns from its catch before calling startDaemon. The revision explicitly retains these behaviors and routes capability/ownership failures into stop failure. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts]","action":"Keep these branches covered while inserting watchdog readiness and serialized cleanup.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed tests exercise the termination and replacement-safety acceptance criteria through observable failures.","evidence":"The planned live-target-after-file-removal case exposes the current waitForStop success condition; blocked-exit testing exercises the missing independent watchdog; retained-handle and replacement tests exercise the current numeric-PID signaling gap. Existing daemon-stop tests fake waitForStop and therefore do not establish these new guarantees. TESTS.md records only the eight foundation tests, consistent with the design's caveat. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-process.test.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-run-files.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/TESTS.md]","action":"Implement the proposed integration cases; retain the distinction between foundation results and acceptance results.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The ac4 investigation record contains the required controlled reproduction and healthy-control evidence.","evidence":"Listed the story documents and read ISSUE.md, BUILD.md and TESTS.md. shutdown-investigation.md is absent; the available results cover process-identity and guard foundations, without blocked-exit reproduction commands, observed deadlines or healthy-watchdog control evidence. The design correctly describes this as future acceptance work. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/TESTS.md, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/BUILD.md]","action":"Create the investigation record and verify every required evidence field before accepting ac4.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T16:27:34.248Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
