641	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"d176315342034132bc682448b3d6572f","actor":{"id":"codex:shutdown-design","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:33:29.534Z","operation":"update","revision":{"number":10,"contentHash":"655cd819ec438f55d0c3e1c6c59d447dbcebd1dcc4a5494fcd6a160c313852d0"},"outcome":{"result":"revised","summary":"Review cycle4 round1: include the implemented shared guard foundation, its tests and the real store-child shutdown fixture in the refinement compatibility audit; distinguish reusable guard serialization from the process signalling that must be replaced."},"addresses":"all"}}
7458	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-24367cb1e4fee92391580c9a9e369094","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:33:32.700Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process capability through stop and adding independent shutdown protection address the ISSUE's two termination defects.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies file-based stop success and a process surviving after 'bye'. stopDaemonWith currently trusts waitForStop before checking a process; createShutdown clears the PID, logs 'bye', clears its backstop, then calls exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained target and independent watchdog cover these separate gaps. The design explicitly defers historical diagnosis rather than claiming it completed. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Implement both protections and retain the explicit historical-diagnosis deferral.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Current CLI and shell stop waits can succeed from run-file disappearance without observing the original process exit.","evidence":"waitForStop returns true on 'if (!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile))'. stopDaemonWith immediately returns '{ stopped: true, forced: false }' from that answer and only rereads the PID after timeout. The shell wait likewise returns zero when PID and socket are absent. createShutdown calls end.clearPid before normal process exit; index.ts starts 'void server.close()' without awaiting it. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"Capture before shutdown and use the retained capability for every subsequent exit decision.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The identified lifecycle, ownership foundations, build integration and store-child fixture are real change sites for the proposed contracts.","evidence":"daemon-process.ts implements signalVerifiedProcess as identity comparison followed by 'kill(target.pid, signal)'. daemon-run-files.ts already supplies mkdir acquisition, owner nonce, fingerprints and orphan diagnostics. IpcServer.listen removes the socket unconditionally; close awaits the server callback and then removes it. store-child calls writePid and createShutdown with 'queue.stop(); void server.close();'. package.json builds with 'tsc && node copy-assets.mjs'; the root copier copies prompts/assets. Caller search found the production writePid/createShutdown wiring in index.ts and the disposable fixture described by the design. [files: src/shared/daemon-process.ts, src/shared/daemon-run-files.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/helpers/store-child.ts, package.json, copy-assets.mjs]","action":"Reconcile these callers together; preserve indirect fatal/startup paths through EndDeps and exitRespectingStoreHealth when ownership cleanup changes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Store-health-aware termination, shutdown reentrancy protection and CLI refusal to restart after a stop error are existing behaviours worth preserving.","evidence":"createShutdown returns immediately after a repeated signal. Its locks-lost paths skip closeStores and call endAfterStoreFailure; that function writes synchronously and invokes killSelf. maintenance.restart catches stopDaemon errors and returns before startDaemon. shutdown-store-failure.test.ts checks healthy drain ordering, repeated signals, lock-loss self-kill and fatal termination; daemon-stop.test.ts checks no start after failed stop. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts]","action":"Keep these regression checks while adding watchdog readiness and guarded close ordering.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Both the control script and CLI already enforce actual process termination before restart, as the preserved-invariants section states.","evidence":"Both waits accept absent run files without checking the original process. Additionally, the shell restart body is 'cmd_stop || true' followed by 'cmd_start'. Thus actual termination before restart is a new guarantee, not an existing invariant. The CLI preserves stop-error propagation, but currently accepts a false successful stop. [files: scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts]","action":"Describe process termination before restart as newly established behaviour. Explicitly require shell cmd_restart and cmd_start to propagate capability/ownership failures and test that neither reaches spawn_daemon after failed stop.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed acceptance coverage is already sufficient to verify ac1–ac4 against implemented behaviour.","evidence":"The design correctly labels the broker/watchdog/platform tests and investigation evidence as future work. Existing daemon-stop tests use a single fixed PID and injected wait result; the eight foundation tests cover identity comparisons and guard primitives, not retained kernel capabilities or complete shutdown/restart wiring. Repository search found no shutdown watchdog/process broker implementation or shutdown-investigation.md. TESTS.md records only the eight foundation tests. Analyzer drill-down was attempted but failed with shaper-llm-unavailable caused by an invalid response schema; direct reads and searches supplied the evidence above. No tests were executed in this read-only review. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-process.test.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-run-files.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/TESTS.md]","action":"Before acceptance, implement and run the planned disposable-process, retained-capability, shell restart-refusal and guarded-close tests; provide the ac4 investigation record. Require Darwin runtime evidence before claiming Darwin support.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":5,"unverified":1},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T17:33:32.700Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
