6740	{"artifactId":"LLD-fd8d70c3e8c397ea-s1","entry":{"id":"review-ee5f6e3bcd40a011a90bc31e29724bee","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-24T17:35:44.367Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Retaining the original process capability through shutdown and independently bounding blocked exit addresses the ISSUE's termination defects.","evidence":"ISSUE.md identifies file-based false success and a process surviving after 'bye'. lifecycle.ts returns true when both files disappear; daemon.ts accepts that result without checking process exit. shutdown.ts clears the PID, logs 'bye', and then invokes process.exit through exitRespectingStoreHealth. The proposed retained target and independent watchdog address those paths. Historical diagnosis is explicitly deferred by the supplied stakeholder decision. [files: docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/ISSUE.md, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts]","action":"Implement the retained-target and watchdog contracts together; keep historical diagnosis explicitly deferred.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CLI and shell currently infer stop from disappearing run files and can lose the original signal target.","evidence":"waitForStop uses `if (!existsSync(PATHS.pidFile) && !existsSync(PATHS.sockFile)) return true`. stopDaemonWith reads livePid again only after waiting. Shell wait_for_daemon_stop similarly succeeds on missing files, while force_stop_daemon rereads PID_FILE. cmd_restart contains `cmd_stop || true` followed by cmd_start. [files: src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh]","action":"Replace file-based success and PID-file rereads with retained-capability exit observation, and propagate shell failures explicitly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed lifecycle sites cover production run-file publication/removal and the disposable store-child shutdown integration.","evidence":"Direct reads and caller searches locate writePid/isAlreadyRunning/clearPid in daemon/lifecycle.ts, unconditional socket removal in IpcServer.listen/close, production shutdown wiring in daemon/index.ts, CLI cleanup in services/daemon.ts and services/lifecycle.ts, and shell cleanup. store-child's daemon-like operation calls writePid and constructs createShutdown with `stopBackgroundWork: () => { queue.stop(); void server.close(); }`. These sites are all included in the design. [files: src/daemon/lifecycle.ts, src/daemon/server.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/fatal.ts, src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/lifecycle.ts, scripts/daemon-ctl.sh, src/db/graph/__tests__/helpers/store-child.ts]","action":"Apply the shared ownership contract across these sites, including EndDeps-based fatal cleanup and existing fixture callers.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Bounded RPC, wait/force-stop phases, StopOutcome compatibility, and restart rejection propagation are existing behavior.","evidence":"daemon.ts bounds shutdown replies at 5 seconds, waits 30 seconds, then verifies the command suffix before SIGKILL and a 5-second exit wait. StopOutcome exposes stopped:true, forced:boolean and optional pid. maintenance.restart catches stop rejection and returns before calling startDaemon. The proposed contract preserves these phases and shape while strengthening their success predicate. [files: src/cli/services/daemon.ts, src/cli/services/maintenance.ts]","action":"Retain the existing outcome shape and restart catch boundary when introducing broker-backed targets.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Store-health-aware no-close/self-kill behavior and shutdown reentrancy protection are real invariants.","evidence":"createShutdown checks `started` before initiating cleanup. With locks-lost health it skips queue draining and closeStores and schedules endAfterStoreFailure. That function writes synchronously and calls killSelf. shutdown-store-failure.test.ts checks repeated signals, skipped close, healthy normal exit, and real disposable lock-loss/fatal exits. [files: src/daemon/shutdown.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/shutdown-store-failure.test.ts, src/db/graph/__tests__/helpers/store-child.ts]","action":"Keep these branches and rerun the real store-child suites after changing watchdog readiness and guarded close ordering.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed test strategy maps every acceptance criterion to a check that distinguishes the fixed behavior from the defect.","evidence":"The supplied design maps ac1 to retained-process survival after file deletion, ac2 to blocked-exit and healthy controls, ac3 to replacement/identity failures and restart refusal, and ac4 to manual controlled-reproduction documentation with a historical-cause caveat. Existing daemon-stop tests cover ordinary force-stop and restart rejection but model natural stop by setting alive=false; they do not establish the new guarantees. TESTS.md records only eight foundation tests, consistent with the design's explicit future-work qualification. [files: src/cli/services/__tests__/daemon-stop.test.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-process.test.ts, src/shared/__tests__/daemon-run-files.test.ts, docs/standalone/daemon-stop-must-wait-process-end-E20261013fd8d70c3/S001/TESTS.md]","action":"Implement the proposed regression and platform tests before acceptance. Produce and inspect shutdown-investigation.md for ac4; the repository currently has no such artifact. Existing foundation results do not prove completion.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":6,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-24T17:35:44.367Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
